cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "patchproof: prove a bounds-check fix eliminates every violating input"
message: "If you use this in academic work, please cite it."
type: software
authors:
  - alias: nickharris808
    website: "https://github.com/nickharris808"
repository-code: "https://github.com/nickharris808/patchproof"
url: "https://huggingface.co/spaces/nickh007/hw-verify"
abstract: >-
  Decides whether a corrected guard admits any input violating a safety relation, at declared machine widths. Discharged twice -- bit-precise with fixed-size bit-vectors, and as a Farkas elimination certificate a third party replays with integer arithmetic and no solver. A certificate is bound to the defect class it claims, so arithmetic that contradicts itself but proves nothing about a patch is reported UNVERIFIED rather than as a pass.
keywords:
  - bounds check
  - farkas lemma
  - certificate
  - formal verification
  - security
license: Apache-2.0
version: "0.1.0"
date-released: "2026-07-28"
